    "explanation": "Correct Choice Analysis: Autonomous System Numbers (ASN), BGP route announcements, and RIR WHOIS queries relate directly to network topology, routing paths, and external IP block allocations, constituting Infrastructure-level footprinting.\nDistractor Analysis:\n- Option A is incorrect because application footprinting analyzes web frameworks, CMS versions, API endpoints, and header metadata.\n- Option B is incorrect because OS fingerprinting uses TCP/IP stack behavior probes (e.g., TTL, TCP window sizes) to identify target operating systems.\n- Option D is incorrect because querying public regional registries (ARIN/RIPE/BGP) is passive OSINT data gathering, not active traffic scanning.",
