    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-00-025",
    "chapterIndex": 0,
    "text": "A corporate enterprise implements a security strategy where external web traffic must pass through a Border Router ACL, an external Next-Generation Firewall (NGFW), a Web Application Firewall (WAF), an isolated DMZ reverse proxy host, and an internal network IDS/IPS before accessing internal application database servers. Furthermore, distinct administrative credentials and multi-factor authentication are enforced at every administrative access tier. What core cyber defense concept does this architectural design embody?",
