    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-00-033",
    "chapterIndex": 0,
    "text": "A corporate employee has authorized access to read files in a shared departmental network drive named `/Finance/Public_Reports`. Using local command line scripts, the employee discovers a permissions misconfiguration that allows them to navigate up one directory level into `/Finance/Restricted_Executive_Salaries` and copy confidential compensation files to a local drive. Under the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA) § 1030, how is this conduct legal categorized?",
