    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-002-034",
    "chapterIndex": 1,
    "text": "During DNS footprinting of `examplecorp.com`, an analyst identifies a CNAME record: `blog.examplecorp.com CNAME webhosting.thirdparty-service.net`. Performing a resolution test reveals that `webhosting.thirdparty-service.net` returns an `NXDOMAIN` status because the third-party account was canceled, but the CNAME record at `examplecorp.com` remains active. What high-severity vulnerability does this DNS footprinting finding expose?",
