    "text": "During an external penetration test against a mid-sized financial services firm, you discover an exposed NFS service listening on port 2049. Running showmount -e against the target reveals several exported directories, including /home and /var/mail with the option 'rw,no_root_squash'. What is the most effective next step to escalate privileges and access sensitive user data?",
