    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-008-054",
    "chapterIndex": 7,
    "text": "A penetration tester physically connects a rogue DHCP server to a wall jack on a corporate network. The server is configured to hand out malicious DNS server IP addresses. However, legitimate clients on that floor continue to receive valid IP configurations from the authorized server. Which security feature is actively preventing the rogue server from operating?",
