    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-008-055",
    "chapterIndex": 7,
    "text": "An attacker wants to intercept the HTTP requests sent from a victim machine to a web server on the internet. To minimize the chance of causing network instability or triggering duplicate MAC address alerts, the attacker decides to only poison the victim's ARP cache, leaving the gateway's cache intact. Which type of sniffing technique is being utilized?",
