    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-008-064",
    "chapterIndex": 7,
    "text": "An attacker successfully executes a MAC flooding attack using `macof`, causing an older switch to fail open and broadcast traffic out of all ports. The attacker then starts Wireshark to capture the traffic but notices they are only seeing broadcast packets and their own traffic, not the unicast traffic between other hosts. What is the most likely reason for this failure?",
