    "explanation": "Correct Choice Analysis: Even if a switch floods unicast traffic out of all ports (acting like a hub), the target host's NIC hardware will still drop any frames whose destination MAC address does not match its own, unless the NIC is explicitly put into promiscuous mode. Without promiscuous mode, the OS never sees the intercepted unicast frames. Distractor Analysis: Option A is incorrect because a failed-open switch floods traffic; it does not isolate ports. Option C is incorrect because CAM table overflow affects all traffic switched locally, regardless of whether it's routed later. Option D is incorrect because a MAC flood targets the switch's CAM table, not the host's ARP cache.",
