    "chapterIndex": 7,
    "text": "An organization discovers that an attacker physically accessed a wiring closet and plugged a laptop into a network hub connecting a critical ICS (Industrial Control System) PLC. The attacker was able to capture all communication between the PLC and the central server without injecting any packets. What is the primary architectural flaw that enabled this passive sniffing?",
