    "text": "A legacy Layer 2 switch has a CAM table capacity of 1024 entries. An attacker begins flooding the switch with forged source MAC addresses. Once the CAM table is completely full, how does the switch handle a legitimate unicast frame arriving on an access port destined for a known, valid MAC address that was recently pushed out of the CAM table?",
