    "correct": 1, // 0-indexed integer corresponding to choices array
    "explanation": "Correct Choice Analysis: This is correct because traditional visual document review relies on the assumption that convincing-looking documents are genuine, but AI-generated synthetic identity documents are specifically engineered to pass this kind of visual scrutiny, meaning organizations need stronger verification methods such as cryptographic signature checks or authoritative database cross-referencing rather than relying on appearance-based review alone.\nDistractor Analysis: The claim about legal exemptions under EC-Council standards is incorrect and fabricated; no such standard exists governing hire verification methods. The claim that AI-generated identity fraud is technically undefeatable is incorrect; layered verification methods (database checks, liveness detection, cryptographic verification) provide meaningful defense. The claim that HR departments are exempt from social engineering risk is incorrect and contradicted by the very incident described in the scenario.",
    "distractors": [
      "Visual review is only legally required for in-person hires, not remote contractors, under EC-Council standards",
      "AI-generated identity fraud is technically impossible to defend against with any current technology",
      "HR departments are exempt from social engineering risk by organizational design"
    ]
