    "chapterIndex": 10,
    "text": "A SOC analyst reviewing proxy logs notices that an attacker first established a TCP connection to a web server, then injected a crafted RST packet with a guessed sequence number, causing the legitimate client’s connection to terminate while the attacker continued communicating with the server using the same session. Which specific network-level technique was employed?",
