    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-011-010",
    "chapterIndex": 10,
    "text": "While testing a mobile banking application, a penetration tester discovers that the OAuth 2.0 bearer tokens issued by the authorization server are accepted by the resource server even after the user has explicitly logged out and the corresponding refresh token has been revoked. Which defensive control is missing?",
