    "text": "An attacker sends a victim a link containing a pre-set session ID: https://app.example.com/login?SESSIONID=ATTACKERCONTROLLED. After the victim authenticates, the attacker uses the same SESSIONID value and gains full access. The application accepted the externally supplied session ID and did not regenerate it upon successful login. Which countermeasure would have prevented this attack?",
