    "text": "A security researcher is analyzing a mobile API that accepts JWT access tokens. The tokens are signed with a publicly known RSA public key, yet the API’s verification routine accepts tokens whose header contains \"alg\": \"none\". An attacker removes the signature and sets the algorithm to none, and the API still grants access. Which token-based attack is demonstrated?",
