    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-012-001",
    "chapterIndex": 11,
    "text": "A penetration tester is engaged by a financial institution to evaluate perimeter defenses. During the engagement the tester observes that the border firewall is a stateful inspection device that tracks the state of TCP connections. The tester needs to send crafted packets that appear to belong to an already-established session in order to reach an internal host. Which technique is most appropriate for this objective?",
