    "text": "A healthcare provider’s web farm uses Apache with multiple name-based virtual hosts. The configuration file contains the directive “ServerName _default_” for the first virtual host and omits an explicit ServerName for several subsequent hosts. During testing, requests that supply an unknown Host header are served the content of the first virtual host, which contains an internal administrative interface. What is the most likely consequence of this misconfiguration?",
