    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-026",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "A penetration tester obtains a memory dump from a compromised embedded router and finds an encrypted configuration blob. The tester also has access to a nearly identical router model in a lab, from which they can derive the exact plaintext template used to generate the configuration blob format, though they cannot inject arbitrary chosen data into the target device. Comparing the known plaintext template against the captured ciphertext to deduce the encryption key represents which cryptanalytic model?",
