    "text": "An attacker targeting a legacy banking API discovers that submitting malformed encrypted session tokens to the token-refresh endpoint causes the server to return different HTTP status codes depending on whether the decrypted token structure was valid, even though the underlying plaintext contents remain hidden. The attacker methodically crafts hundreds of token variants and observes these status code differences to incrementally decrypt a legitimate captured token. Which cryptanalytic model is illustrated?",
