    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-030",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "A security team managing a document notarization platform generates a SHA-1 digest for every uploaded contract to detect tampering. An internal red team demonstrates that they can generate two distinct PDF files, one benign and one containing altered payment routing details, that both produce the identical SHA-1 digest, thereby defeating the integrity check without needing to know the digest algorithm's internal secret key (since it has none). This demonstration relies primarily on which mathematical principle?",
