    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-031",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "A SOC analyst reviewing a leaked credential dump notices that identical plaintext passwords across different user accounts always produce identical hash values in the exposed database. The analyst concludes that an attacker could build a single precomputed dataset of hash-to-plaintext mappings once and reuse it against the entire dataset. What underlying storage design flaw enables this efficiency for the attacker?",
