    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-032",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "During an internal red team exercise, an operator gains read access to a HashiCorp Vault-adjacent secrets store and discovers thousands of unsalted MD5 password hashes. Rather than generating collisions or querying an oracle, the operator downloads a well-known 15GB precomputed dataset optimized for reversing MD5 hashes up to 9 characters using time-memory tradeoff chains. What is this technique properly called, and why is it effective here?",
