    "text": "A financial services firm allows employees to reset forgotten application passwords through a legacy help desk portal. A security researcher notices that when submitting incorrect password guesses, the server's response time is measurably longer for guesses that get the first few characters correct compared to entirely wrong guesses, suggesting a non-constant-time string comparison function is used internally. Which category of vulnerability does this represent, and what is the appropriate fix?",
