    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-035",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "An internal audit of an organization's internal PKI reveals that a subordinate CA certificate used to sign employee authentication certificates expired eleven months ago. Despite this, the domain controller continues to accept authentication requests signed by certificates chaining up to the expired subordinate CA because certificate expiration checking was disabled during a troubleshooting session two years prior and never re-enabled. What is the MOST significant risk this configuration introduces?",
