    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-039",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "A managed service provider inherits a client's aging e-commerce platform and discovers the web server still negotiates SSL v2 connections for compatibility with an internal legacy inventory system. A researcher demonstrates that SSL v2's weak message authentication design allows an active attacker to strip cipher suite options during the handshake, forcing the connection into using export-grade 40-bit encryption regardless of the client's actual capabilities. What is the most appropriate remediation strategy?",
