    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-045",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "A government contractor's legacy VPN concentrator still supports 512-bit export-grade Diffie-Hellman parameters for backward compatibility with equipment purchased in the late 1990s. A nation-state-level adversary is believed to have the computational resources to precompute discrete logarithms for commonly used primes at this key strength, potentially allowing them to passively decrypt large volumes of previously captured traffic. What is the most appropriate long-term remediation the contractor should pursue?",
