    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "A cryptanalyst working for a national CERT is given access to an air-gapped appliance and permitted to submit any plaintext of their choosing through its front panel test interface, receiving the ciphertext output for each submission. However, the appliance's decryption function is completely inaccessible; only the encryption path can be exercised. The analyst is trying to determine whether the block cipher mode used leaks structural information about repeating plaintext blocks. Which cryptanalytic model governs this evaluation?",
