    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-055",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "A cloud storage provider notices that two customer-uploaded files, submitted independently by unrelated users months apart, produce identical SHA-1 hash values despite having completely different byte content. Internal investigation confirms this was not a system error but a deliberately engineered collision. What underlying probabilistic concept explains why finding such a collision requires dramatically fewer computational attempts than finding a specific pre-image matching a given target hash?",
