    "text": "An enterprise PKI team discovers that a self-signed certificate is being used on an internal API gateway that handles sensitive payroll data, and that client applications connecting to this gateway have certificate pinning disabled along with certificate chain validation entirely bypassed in a hardcoded configuration flag left over from initial development testing. What is the most complete and appropriate remediation the team should implement?",
