    "text": "A SOC analyst reviewing network traffic logs identifies a pattern where a client repeatedly initiates TLS handshakes to the same server, each time having its connection reset shortly after the ClientHello message, followed immediately by a successful connection using an older, weaker protocol version. This pattern recurs dozens of times over a short period for the same client-server pair. What is the MOST likely explanation for this traffic pattern, and what should the analyst investigate next?",
