    "id": "CEH-V13-CQ-020-076",
    "chapterIndex": 19,
    "text": "A cryptography instructor presents students with a scenario: an attacker has compromised a satellite communication relay and can now inject arbitrary plaintext messages of their choosing into the encryption pipeline before they are transmitted, observing the resulting ciphertext for each injected message, with the goal of eventually recovering the block cipher's internal key schedule. No decryption capability is available to the attacker at any point. Which model correctly classifies this scenario?",
